cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite vc-linux, please cite it as below."
title: "vc-linux: preserving DOS software by translation, not emulation"
abstract: >-
  Volkov Commander, GW-BASIC and other DOS programs, kept as their original unedited source, a
  reproducible build, and a machine translation from 8086 assembly to C checked instruction by
  instruction. DOS and the PC hardware are reimplemented, so the programs run natively on Linux
  and as WebAssembly in any browser.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Oleynik
    given-names: Evgeny
repository-code: "https://github.com/evoleinik/vc-linux"
url: "https://notanemulator.com/"
license: BSD-2-Clause
keywords:
  - software preservation
  - static recompilation
  - binary translation
  - DOS
  - "8086"
  - Volkov Commander
  - WebAssembly
references:
